{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"bf32b491-561f-4561-9a3f-fbb5049bd23f","title":"The centroid is where the medians of a triangle meet"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf32b491-561f-4561-9a3f-fbb5049bd23f","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A median joins a vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side. Here, M splits side AB into two equal lengths.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Where do medians meet?"},{"op":"figure","id":"triangle","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.6,6.6],"y":[-0.7,5.2],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[0,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[6,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[1.5,4.5],"label":"C"},{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"point","id":"m","at":{"mid":["a","b"]},"label":"M"},{"kind":"segment","id":"cm","from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"m"}},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"m"},"label":"3"},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"m"},"to":{"at":"b"},"label":"3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"midpoint","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"AM=MB\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad CM\\text{ is a median}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf32b491-561f-4561-9a3f-fbb5049bd23f","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Now draw medians from the other two vertices. All three pass through the same point, called the centroid.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"medians","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"n","at":{"mid":["b","c"]},"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"mid":["a","c"]},"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","id":"an","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"n"}},{"kind":"segment","id":"bp","from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"p"}},{"kind":"point","id":"g","at":{"hit":["cm","an"]},"label":"G"}]},{"op":"text","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"midpoint","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"G is the centroid: all three medians meet."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf32b491-561f-4561-9a3f-fbb5049bd23f","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The centroid divides every median in a two-to-one ratio. The longer part is always next to the vertex.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"ratio_marks","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"g"},"label":"2 parts"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"g"},"to":{"at":"m"},"label":"1 part"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"ratio","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"CG:GM=AG:GN=BG:GP=2:1"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If median CM is 12 cm long, how far is the centroid G from vertex C?","expected_gist":"CG is two-thirds of CM, so CG = 8 cm."}}}
